/workspace/jieran/APROF/aprof/.aprof/runs/level2-skill-graph-base-20261005-experiment/train/tasks/gcd/feedback/gcd001-reclassification-01.json", "sha256": "sha256:ad249c10fd6ae7b0026a47ce1c234510eeb4917d333f9ce6c9a8a950eb28f892"}], "future_rounds_authored": false, "graph_hash": "sha256:4d18205d52b089bce811dedfa3508ad0605d19d33fdcdb7f59109a043b7261aa", "implementation_source_hash": "sha256:6aa97e5a3ba2bf1ab2e9f98780a0196f653c1e817254e6813276426377e8cab0", "operator": "gcd", "optimization_stage": "algorithm_parallel", "parallel_plan_ref": "sha256:85b9af645e02ae8a7c8b5fd2ee17f2f753709ebd0fd6d769996992fbbca7bd5d", "plan_basis_source_hash": "sha256:973b7711cc879fbc28558c30ef084147149c25ce10e4865c660485a8e284ec29", "predictions": [{"basis": "Single writer for tiny outputs; original Euclidean arithmetic retained.", "cases": "all20_plus_boundary_guards", "direction": "pass", "metric": "correctness"}, {"basis": "All public search cases are larger than 256 elements and retain baseline tiling.", "cases": [1, 8, 14, 20], "direction": "unchanged", "metric": "paired_complete_call_time"}], "rationale": "GCD001 closed feedback proves exact integer boundary mismatches on tiny outputs. A six-element boundary launched six blocks and neighboring output words became zero despite successful dispatch. Small stores from separate blocks may overlap a hardware store granule. One block isolates that ownership hypothesis without changing Euclidean arithmetic. The pre-registration gcd002 draft could not satisfy the frozen same-shape key1 boundary guard with fallback-only dispatch; this revised unregistered source routes both keys to the original kernel without adding a computation change. The v2 materialization omitted protected baseline package files and failed pre-registration; this package restores them byte-identically. The v3 materialization retained the old key1 sequence label, so the pre-registration launcher check rejected it; v4 binds both keys to the same actual gcd_kernel. The v4 pre-registration ledger check required the closed observation ID as a string decision basis; this revision binds it without changing source.", "source_dir": "/mnt/tidalfs-hwwh01/dataset/dots_infra/workspace/jieran/APROF/aprof/.aprof/runs/level2-skill-graph-base-20261005-experiment/train/tasks/gcd/candidates/gcd002v5/op", "source_parent": "baseline", "statement": "Use one block for GCD outputs of at most 256 elements, keeping baseline Euclidean arithmetic and original large-output partition. The same-shape key selects the same gcd_kernel entry for frozen guard compatibility."}
